  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNFPA Sexual and reproductive health and rights 2017-2020 - UNFPA Sexual and reproductive health and rights 2017-2020 incl COVID-19 response</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNFPA Sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa och r&#xe4;ttigheter 2017-2020</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen &#xe4;r ett st&#xf6;d till UNFPAs landprogram i Etiopien 2017-2020 f&#xf6;r deras arbete med sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa och r&#xe4;ttigheter, och genom avtals&#xe4;ndringen planerar Sverige att tillf&#xf6;ra medel f&#xf6;r att bidra till UNFPA:s respons p&#xe5; Covid-19 epedemin i Etiopien.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This contribution is a support to UNFPA&apos;s country programme in Ethiopia 2017-2020, with the aim to strengthen access and quality of sexual and reproductive health and rights, and through an amendment to the agreement Sweden is planning to add funds for 2020 in order to scale up the contribution to the UNFPA:s response to Covid-19.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives of the UNFPA country programme for Ethiopia 2016-2020 focus on: SRHR (including HIV), adolescents and youth, gender equality and women&#x2019;s economic empowerment, and population dynamics.
However, due to the spread of Covid-19 in Ethiopia, and the already noted and further expected negative consequences of the pandemic in terms of limiting access to SRHR, increasing GBV, and, placing a very heavy burden on the national health system, additional objectives for 2020 are included:
-Ensuring continuity of access to SRHR services during the Covid-19 pandemic.
-Addressing GBV, including strengthening health facilities and safe houses and access to them.
-Ensuring a continuous supply of contraceptives and reproductive health services.
-Promoting youth engagement for SRHR, and &#x2018;leaving no one behind&#x2019;. Promoting communication on risks due to Covid-19, and community engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
